{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f1334f5b7e0c0d679c04a7d84885442c501324169e17fa25fb5a923521292cf4","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot entry storage and reducer cache","key_entities":["reducer/_api.py:221","reducer/_cache.py:196","reducer/_processors.py:58","write_cache",".cache.json","tickets-<sha>/","_store/fsutil.py:96","atomic_write","janitor.reverify_entry","in_snapshot_entry","_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","os.replace","ADR 0005 D2"],"problem_keywords":["immutability","snapshot entries","cache writes","content-addressed storage","read-side mutations","store corruption","inode sharing"],"propositions":["Snapshot entries documented as immutable are mutated by every ticket read, which writes .cache.json inside the entry directory","The reducer cache write sites (reducer/_api.py and reducer/_processors.py) call write_cache with cache_path pointing inside the snapshot entry, causing post-materialization file mutations","Entry reverification fails because the baseline digest becomes stale after subsequent reads add .cache.json files, causing entries to be incorrectly evicted as corrupt","Reliance on atomic_write's os.replace implementation (rather than in-place write) masks the immutability violation; a future in-place write would silently corrupt inodes shared between entries"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787552310877191001,"uuid":"aaa0525d-25f3-4fe0-a753-3173f3678116"}